om/users/jobfynder/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jobfynder/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created":false,"deleted":false,"base_ref":null,"compare":"https://github.com/jobfynder/hermes/compare/6b7319af125e...91d5e520c9ed","commits":[{"id":"91d5e520c9edea7ff539cd57649ce1c0ad1192a7","tree_id":"313a52f34e77bce0e01e591f6b66ee4cc03e25a7","distinct":true,"message":"fix(reporting): filter structurally-noisy terms out of top job titles\n\nFollow-up to the Recruitment Intelligence report. Verified the new\ntop_job_titles output against real production data and found the\nsame class of contamination already fixed for top_skills: \"DATA\"\n(2,438) and \"Contract\" (1,369) ranked in the top 5 titles -- neither\nis a job title.\n\nget_recruitment_intelligence's top_job_titles now filters through\n_is_noise_job_title() the same way top_skills already filters through\n_is_noise_skill_term(), over-fetching 3x and taking the first `limit`\nsurvivors. Documented plainly in the docstring that this filter\ncatches structurally-malformed strings (fragments, verb phrases,\nencoding junk) and will NOT catch a single real word that's simply\nmisclassified -- \"Contract\" reads like an employment_type value\nleaking into job_title, which is a classifier/taxonomy accuracy\nquestion, not something safe to silently filter out of a report\nwithout risking hiding a real bug. Left visible for now.\n\nNew regression test: top_job_titles must never include a term\n_is_noise_job_title() would reject. Full suite (27 checks) passes\nagainst a fresh schema and freshly built image.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","timestamp":"2026-09-02T19:22:55-04:00","url":"https://github.com/jobfynder/hermes/commit/91d5e520c9edea7ff539cd57649ce1c0ad1192a7","author":{"name":"Jobfynder Automation","email":"automation@jobfynder.com","date":"2026-09-02T19:22:55-04:00"},"committer":{"name":"Jobfynder Automation","email":"automation@jobfynder.com","date":"2026-09-02T19:22:55-04:00"},"added":[],"removed":[],"modified":["app/reporting/service.py","scripts/hermes-950-reporting-assistant-check.py"]}],"head_commit":{"id":"91d5e520c9edea7ff539cd57649ce1c0ad1192a7","tree_id":"313a52f34e77bce0e01e591f6b66ee4cc03e25a7","distinct":true,"message":"fix(reporting): filter structurally-noisy terms out of top job titles\n\nFollow-up to the Recruitment Intelligence report. Verified the new\ntop_job_titles output against real production data and found the\nsame class of contamination already fixed for top_skills: \"DATA\"\n(2,438) and \"Contract\" (1,369) ranked in the top 5 titles -- neither\nis a job title.\n\nget_recruitment_intelligence's top_job_titles now filters through\n_is_noise_job_title() the same way top_skills already filters through\n_is_noise_skill_term(), over-fetching 3x and taking the first `limit`\nsurvivors. Documented plainly in the docstring that this filter\ncatches structurally-malformed strings (fragments, verb phrases,\nencoding junk) and will NOT catch a single real word that's simply\nmisclassified -- \"Contract\" reads like an employment_type value\nleaking into job_title, which is a classifier/taxonomy accuracy\nquestion, not something safe to silently filter out of a report\nwithout risking hiding a real bug. Left visible for now.\n\nNew regression test: top_job_titles must never include a term\n_is_noise_job_title() would reject. Full suite (27 checks) passes\nagainst a fresh schema and freshly built image.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","timestamp":"2026-09-02T19:22:55-04:00","url":"https://github.com/jobfynder/hermes/commit/91d5e520c9edea7ff539cd57649ce1c0ad1192a7","author":{"name":"Jobfynder Automation","email":"automation@jobfynder.com","date":"2026-09-02T19:22:55-04:00"},"committer":{"name":"Jobfynder Automation","email":"automation@jobfynder.com","date":"2026-09-02T19:22:55-04:00"},"added":[],"removed":[],"modified":["app/reporting/service.py","scripts/hermes-950-reporting-assistant-check.py"]}}
